  "observations": "Personally inspected all three current assembly views with both assets loaded. North-up shows the complete separate sanctuary court/stupa and the ten-room estimated annex without overlap; opposite oblique shows both bodies on the hillside. The south oblique source slope occludes much of the lower annex and sanctuary. These modern coarse DEM intersections and unverified seventh-century benches remain disclosed. The annex uses original modest plinths and estimated room architecture; exact census, layout, facing, sections and finishes are not surveyed. Story coordinate is approximate and differs roughly1.4km from the current Wikipedia point. Historical member dates650/700CE are retained as estimates, with assembly700CE, not a certified simultaneous state. All imagery unused. Existing sanctuary geometry, field, floor, sections and QA are unchanged.",
